## What to look for
- The agent introduces the business, reads a disclosure, asks for verification, quotes amounts or dues, or offers help.
- The customer states a need, asks about their own account, answers verification questions, objects, or asks to be called back.

## Output
Return json only. Give every speaker label in the transcript exactly one role: "agent" or "caller" ("caller" is the customer). If the transcript has two speakers, one must be "agent" and the other "caller".
confidence is "high" when the content clearly shows the roles, "medium" when it leans one way, "low" when you are guessing.
reason is at most 200 characters.
Example shape (values are illustrative only):
{"speaker_roles": {"spk_0": "agent", "spk_1": "caller"}, "confidence": "high", "reason": "spk_0 greets on behalf of the bank and quotes an EMI due."}
